@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+# V4.1 Hopper BF16 indexer
+
+Adapted from FlashInfer commit
+`b9455a23c6cb63894b28c878e6290fec7899d48b`, directory
+`flashinfer/experimental/qwen_3_5_block/_cudnn_frost/`.
+The upstream SM90 producer/consumer WGMMA pipeline is retained. Local changes
+add a dense BF16 score mode with BF16 rounding after QK, multiplication and
+head reduction. The SGLang caller retains causal masks, candidate selection,
+top-k, and paging. FP4 quantization is unchanged.
+
+Public entry: `sglang.kernels.ops.attention.dsv4.sm90_indexer.sm90_indexer_scores`.
+Runtime opt-in: `SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_SM90_INDEXER=1` on SM90. Unsupported shapes
+continue using the original model path. The request scorer increases fused
+query tiles to at most 1024 rows, with a 1 GiB budget accounting for output,
+causal masks, masked copies and the preceding yielded chunk. Compilation errors
+are surfaced rather
+than silently falling back, so a successful test proves the kernel ran.
+
+The imported helpers retain their original copyright and SPDX notices.
+`LICENSE.Apache-2.0` and `LICENSE.FlashAttention` preserve the upstream Apache
+and MIT license texts. The upstream helper comments refer to licensing documents
+that were absent from the pinned FlashInfer tree; those references are not
+additional imported files. See the pinned source and these license texts.
+
+This backend is under numerical and performance validation. It does not claim
+bitwise equivalence for arbitrary floating-point input ranges: GEMM and reduction
+orders can differ, even with matching BF16 rounding boundaries.
+
+## Attention boundary on Hopper TP8
+
+`SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_SM90_ATTN_MHC_ALL_REDUCE=1` opts into the existing CUDA
+all-reduce + mHC post + combine + RMSNorm epilogue for the V4.1 attention
+boundary on SM90 TP8. The model registers its CustomAllReduceV2 communicator
+before graph capture. Only 1–16 rows with sufficient push-plane capacity are
+admitted; larger batches, CP, attention DP, unsupported norms and unavailable
+communicators retain the existing path. MoE collective fusion is not enabled
+by this flag. An enabled flag does not prove the model took the fused path;
+check the actual kernel trace before attributing a serving speedup to it.
+
+The reproducible eight-GPU acceptance/microbenchmark is
+`test/manual/kernels/communication/bench_dsv41_sm90_mhc.py`. Its comparator is
+CustomAllReduceV2 plus separate mHC post and combine/norm kernels. Model E2E
+is needed to compare against serving's FlashInfer all-reduce. These optimization
+flags default off while deployment-specific E2E acceptance is established.
+
+## DeepSelect prefill
+
+`SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_SM90_DEEPSELECT_PREFILL=1` enables the existing SGLang
+DeepSelect implementation for full token selection in full-top-k and
+candidate-publishing layers on Hopper. The scorer emits BF16 directly when
+this flag is enabled; values were already rounded to BF16 before the original
+FP32 store. The optional output dtype is part of the compiled-kernel cache key.
+Both output formats now allocate 128-byte aligned rows and padded final-row
+storage. Causal masking is in place so it preserves that layout.
+
+DeepSelect receives the device-side row lengths, emits ascending int32 indices,
+and skips value output. Out-of-range indices use the request width as sentinel
+until writeback replaces them with -1. This preserves both raw compressed
+positions and pool-slot outputs without a second index sort. Short, unaligned,
+or unsupported top-k shapes use torch. Candidate block selection and selection
+within published blocks retain their existing algorithms.
+
+The synthetic chain benchmark is
+`test/manual/kernels/attention/bench_dsv41_deepselect_prefill.py`. It includes
+masking or layout conversion, selection, sorting and both index writes. Native
+BF16 results assume the producer already provides aligned BF16 scores; they
+are not a model E2E speedup. Runtime tests cover short rows, zero lengths,
+odd widths, ties, nonconsecutive output rows, optional page output and
+changed-length CUDA Graph replay.
+
+## Causal prefill work and writeback
+
+`SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_SM90_PREFILL_IO=1`, together with the DeepSelect flag,
+trims each score tile's K prefix to its largest visible length (rounded up to
+64 columns, retaining at least top-k columns). The per-request CPU lengths
+are collected once before iterating tiles. Future scores are masked in place
+without materializing a comparison tensor. One Triton launch writes sorted
+indices to both raw positions and optional page slots, including invalid tails.
+The public wrappers live in `ops.attention.dsv4.sm90_prefill_io`.
+
+This remains opt-in pending full-model performance validation. The trimming
+uses the eager request planner; graph replay of the device-only mask/write
+kernels does not imply the whole request planner is graph-capturable.
+
+`SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_SM90_PREFILL_MHC=1` admits Hopper to the existing CUDA
+post/combine/RMSNorm prefill epilogue. It retains BF16 intermediate boundaries,
+the 4096–65536-row and 5120-hidden-size limits, four streams, and the existing
+norm eligibility checks. CP and attention DP keep their original path.
